{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-84713" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the horizontal parabola given by the Cartesian equation ${y}^{2}=8x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-84713" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of a horizontal parabola ${y}^{2}=4px$ that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=p{t}^{2},\\,y=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing the given Cartesian equation with the general case ${y}^{2}=4px$ and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4px & =8x \\\\ 4p & =8 \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=(2){t}^{2},\\,y=2(2)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=2{t}^{2},\\,y=4t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-84713" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a67ea273ef0cb0349fa2737d67de87544f259bda79792a0d407c2cb6c1f45894"} {"question" "q-84713" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-84713" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=2{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=2t"] ["math" "x=2{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=4t"] ["math" "x=4{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=4t"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=4t"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-84713" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=2{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=4t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-84716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/assets/85894c676349da1794c2b4e3ab3add867fbe9e91037bee060e3592039c3850cf.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-84716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The diagram shows that the parabola is horizontal, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(-4,4).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a horizontal parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=p{t}^{2},\\,y=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(-4,4),$ we can substitute $x=-4$ and $y=4$ into the standard parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-4=p{t}^{2} \\\\ 4=2pt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the second equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =2pt \\\\ 2 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{2}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & =p{(\\frac{2}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -4 & =p\\cdot \\frac{4}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{4}{p} \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=(-1){t}^{2},\\,y=2(-1)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=-{t}^{2},\\,y=-2t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-84716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a67ea273ef0cb0349fa2737d67de87544f259bda79792a0d407c2cb6c1f45894"} {"question" "q-84716" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-84716" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-2t,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}"] ["math" "x=-2{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=-t"] ["math" "x=-{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=-2t"] ["math" "x=-{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=-t"] ["math" "x=2t,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-84716" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=-{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=-2t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-84732" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=3{t}^{2},\\,y=6t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-84732" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{x}{3},\\,t=\\frac{y}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=\\frac{x}{3}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =\\frac{x}{3} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =12x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian equation of the parabola is ${y}^{2}=12x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-84732" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a67ea273ef0cb0349fa2737d67de87544f259bda79792a0d407c2cb6c1f45894"} {"question" "q-84732" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-84732" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{2}=12x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=6x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-84732" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=12x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-106421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the horizontal parabola given by the Cartesian equation ${y}^{2}=16x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-106421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of a horizontal parabola ${y}^{2}=4px$ that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=p{t}^{2},\\,y=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing the given Cartesian equation with the general case ${y}^{2}=4px$ and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4px & =16x \\\\ 4p & =16 \\\\ p & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=(4){t}^{2},\\,y=2(4)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=4{t}^{2},\\,y=8t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-106421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a67ea273ef0cb0349fa2737d67de87544f259bda79792a0d407c2cb6c1f45894"} {"question" "q-106421" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-106421" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=2{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=4t"] ["math" "x=4t,\\,\\,y=4{t}^{2}"] ["math" "x=4{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=8t"] ["math" "x=8t,\\,\\,y=4{t}^{2}"] ["math" "x=8{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=8t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-106421" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=4{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=8t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-280361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following parabola:\n\n$$\nx=-2t,\\,y=-\\frac{4}{3}{t}^{2},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of the parabola is\n\n${x}^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-280361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =-\\frac{x}{2},\\,{t}^{2}=-\\frac{3y}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-\\frac{3y}{4}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =-\\frac{3y}{4} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-3y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian equation of the parabola is ${x}^{2}=-3y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-280361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a67ea273ef0cb0349fa2737d67de87544f259bda79792a0d407c2cb6c1f45894"} {"question" "q-280361" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"} {"question" "q-280361" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/state.json" "file_sha256" "a831258f0950046cfa52561363a0559bb67cd5d484dccc015b4a87750479b2a6"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1207 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
